.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt MK.TOOLCHAIN.MSVC.MK 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mk.toolchain.msvc.mk
.Nd the MSVC runtime, with cl.exe or clang
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Read when
.Va TOOLCHAIN Ns = Ns Cm msvc ,
or
.Va TOOLCHAIN Ns = Ns Cm llvm Va ABI Ns = Ns Cm msvc ,
which compiles with clang-cl and links with lld-link against the same MSVC
headers and libraries.
Both build only on a Windows host with Cygwin.
.Pp
.Va CC
is
.Pa scripts/msvc-cc-wrapper.sh ,
which takes the usual compiler options and passes them on in cl.exe's syntax, so
makefiles need no MSVC branches.
.Va LD , AR , AS
and
.Va RANLIB
are set to match;
.Va AS
may be overridden.
.Pp
Not included directly by a makefile.
.Pp
If cl.exe is on
.Ev PATH ,
that environment is used as it is; otherwise
.Xr mk.vcvarsall.mk 5
finds one.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
Exported to the wrapper:
.Bl -tag -width "BMK_MSVC_INCLUDE"
.It Ev BMK_MSVC_BIN
The toolset's directory.
.It Ev BMK_MSVC_INCLUDE , BMK_MSVC_LIB
Its headers and libraries.
.It Ev BMK_MSVC_CL , BMK_MSVC_LIBEXE
With clang: what replaces cl.exe and lib.exe.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl $ bmake TOOLCHAIN=msvc
.Dl $ bmake TOOLCHAIN=llvm ABI=msvc BMK_EWDK_ROOT='F:\e'
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It TOOLCHAIN=msvc cannot cross-compile
MSVC only targets Windows, from Windows.
Use
.Va TOOLCHAIN Ns = Ns Cm llvm
for mingw-w64 output.
.It cl.exe was found on PATH but lib.exe was not
.Ev PATH
is only partly set up.
.It TOOLCHAIN=llvm ABI=msvc needs clang-cl and lld-link on PATH
On Cygwin they come with the clang and lld packages.
.El
.Sh CAVEATS
Only the
.Cm address
sanitizer exists.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bmake-it 7 ,
.Xr mk.common.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.toolchain.llvm.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.vcvarsall.mk 5
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Sylvain Souche
